;; Home-layer subagent overrides, symlinked to ~/.agents/subagents by the dotfiles
;; `agents.nix`. This is the middle link of the config chain:
;;   packaged skills/herdr-orch/subagents/config.edn
;;     <- this file (~/.agents/subagents/config.edn)
;;       <- project <git-root>/.agents/subagents/config.edn
;;
;; `merge-config` is `merge-with merge`, so a `:harnesses` entry here REPLACES the
;; packaged entry for that kind wholesale rather than merging its keys. Every entry
;; below must therefore restate `:model-flag`; omitting it fails validation at parse
;; with this file's path.
;;
;; WHY: Claude Code and Codex both default to interactive per-command approval, so a
;; spawned subagent stalls at its first tool call waiting for a human who is not
;; watching its pane. The parent then reports a timeout while the child sits blocked.
;; These flags make non-interactive delegation possible for those two harnesses.
;;
;; CHOICE OF MODE -- bounded autonomy, not a blanket bypass:
;;
;; claude `--permission-mode auto` classifies each action against shipped rules
;; (17 allow / 65 soft-deny / 1 hard-deny on Claude Code 2.1.220, inspectable via
;; `claude auto-mode config`). Ordinary subagent work is in `allow`: read-only
;; operations, local file operations within project scope, installing already-declared
;; dependencies, and pushing to the session repo. Genuinely dangerous actions --
;; force push, production deploy, `curl | bash`, mass deletion -- stay in soft-deny and
;; still escalate, which is the point: an unattended child should stall on those rather
;; than proceed. `bypassPermissions` was rejected: it disables the checks wholesale and
;; additionally blocks on its own startup confirmation, so it stalls anyway.
;; `acceptEdits` was rejected as too narrow -- it clears file edits but still prompts for
;; every Bash command, which is most of what a subagent does.
;;
;; codex has no single equivalent, so the two axes are set to match that intent:
;; `-a never` (no approval prompts) with `--sandbox workspace-write` (writes confined to
;; the workspace). `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` was rejected for the same
;; reason as `bypassPermissions`: it removes the sandbox as well as the prompts, which is
;; a far larger grant than "do not ask me".
;;
;; RISK: every claude- and codex-kind subagent runs commands unprompted in the caller's
;; worktree, on every project on this machine. Bounded by claude's deny rules and codex's
;; workspace sandbox, but still a real grant: do not copy this onto a shared or
;; internet-exposed host. `pi` is intentionally omitted -- it does not suffer this
;; approval stall, so granting it anything would widen the blast radius for nothing.
;;
;; Verified against Claude Code 2.1.220 and codex-cli 0.145.0.

{:harnesses {:claude {:model-flag "--model"
                      :extra-args ["--permission-mode" "auto"]}
             :codex  {:model-flag "--model"
                      :extra-args ["--ask-for-approval" "never"
                                   "--sandbox" "workspace-write"]}}}
